<% content_for :title, "Connect your agents" %>
<% hook = "~/.config/multitasking/agent-hook" %>

<%= page_title "Connect your agents",
      description: "When Claude Code or Codex finishes a turn or needs you, a task lands in #{current_team.name}’s list, filed under the repository’s project. Ping it again and the same task bounces back to the top." %>

<div class="split">
  <div class="stack--loose stack">
    <section class="stack">
      <h2>1. Install the hook</h2>
      <p class="muted">Run this once on each machine you use an agent on. It downloads the hook and saves your token beside it, so the token never sits in a settings file you might share.</p>
      <div data-controller="clipboard">
        <pre data-clipboard-target="source">mkdir -p ~/.config/multitasking && curl -fsSL <%= agent_hook_url %> -o <%= hook %> && chmod +x <%= hook %> && printf 'url=<%= request.base_url %>\ntoken=<%= current_team.inbox_token %>\n' > ~/.config/multitasking/config && chmod 600 ~/.config/multitasking/config</pre>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-clipboard-target="button" data-action="clipboard#copy">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>2. Claude Code</h2>
      <p class="muted">Add this to <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code>. <code>Stop</code> fires when Claude finishes a turn; <code>Notification</code> fires when it is waiting on you; <code>PreToolUse</code> fires when it stops mid-turn to ask you a question.</p>
      <div data-controller="clipboard">
        <pre data-clipboard-target="source"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(
              "hooks" => {
                "Stop" => [ { "hooks" => [ { "type" => "command", "command" => "#{hook} claude" } ] } ],
                "Notification" => [ { "hooks" => [ { "type" => "command", "command" => "#{hook} claude" } ] } ],
                "PreToolUse" => [ { "matcher" => "AskUserQuestion|ExitPlanMode",
                                    "hooks" => [ { "type" => "command", "command" => "#{hook} claude" } ] } ]
              }
            ) %></pre>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-clipboard-target="button" data-action="clipboard#copy">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>3. Codex</h2>
      <p class="muted">Add this line to <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>. Codex calls it after every turn. It goes through <code>sh</code> because Codex does not expand <code>~</code>.</p>
      <div data-controller="clipboard">
        <pre data-clipboard-target="source">notify = ["sh", "-c", "exec <%= hook %> codex \"$1\"", "sh"]</pre>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-clipboard-target="button" data-action="clipboard#copy">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>4. Browser tabs</h2>
      <p class="muted">Drag this to your bookmarks bar. Click it on any page and that tab opens here as a task, title and link filled in. Works in any browser, with your sign-in, no token.</p>
      <p><%= link_to "Save tab", tab_bookmarklet, class: "btn btn--sm", draggable: true %></p>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>5. Slack</h2>
      <% if @slack %>
        <p class="muted">Connected to <%= @slack.slack_team_name.presence || "your Slack" %>. React to any message with 📌 <code>:<%= SlackConnection::EMOJI %>:</code> and it lands here, linked back to the message. Pin it again after ticking it off and it comes back. Or copy a message’s link in Slack and paste it into the quick-add box.</p>
        <p><%= button_to "Disconnect Slack", slack_connection_path, method: :delete, class: "btn btn--sm btn--ghost" %></p>
      <% elsif SlackConnection.configured? %>
        <p class="muted">React to any message with 📌 <code>:<%= SlackConnection::EMOJI %>:</code> and it lands here, linked back to the message. Or paste a message’s link into the quick-add box. Each person connects their own Slack. Done reads only the messages you pin or paste.</p>
        <p><%= button_to "Connect Slack", slack_connection_path, class: "btn btn--sm", form: { data: { turbo: false } } %></p>
      <% elsif policy(current_team).update? %>
        <p class="muted">Slack is not set up yet. Create a Slack app at <code>api.slack.com/apps</code> → <em>From a manifest</em>, and paste this. Then put its client id, client secret and signing secret in credentials under <code>slack:</code>. See README.md.</p>
        <div data-controller="clipboard">
          <pre data-clipboard-target="source"><%= slack_manifest %></pre>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-clipboard-target="button" data-action="clipboard#copy">Copy</button>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <p class="muted">Slack is not set up yet. Ask a team admin.</p>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>Anything else</h2>
      <p class="muted">Any tool can post JSON to the inbox. Send the same <code>external_id</code> twice and it updates one task. Send a <code>directory</code> and the task is filed under that folder’s <%= link_to "project", projects_path %>.</p>
      <pre>curl -X POST <%= inbox_tasks_url %> \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Reply to Sam","source":"slack","url":"https://…","external_id":"C123-1712"}'</pre>
    </section>
  </div>

  <aside class="panel panel--sunken">
    <div class="panel__header"><h2>Inbox token</h2></div>
    <p class="muted">Anyone with this token can add tasks to this team. Nothing else.</p>
    <% if policy(current_team).update? %>
      <p style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">
        <%= button_to "Make a new token", connection_path, method: :patch, class: "btn btn--sm",
              form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "The old token stops working at once. Carry on?" } } %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </aside>
</div>
